From: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Subject: MAINTAINERS: classify kmemleak as an MM component
Date: Sun, 01 Nov 2026 18:30:41 -0800

Rename KMEMLEAK to MEMORY MANAGEMENT - KMEMLEAK and move the entry between
KASAN and KSM.  Kmemleak detects kernel memory leaks and belongs with the
other MM components.

Keep Catalin Marinas as maintainer and retain the Maintained status and all
four file patterns.  Add linux-mm@kvack.org to the entry so patches for
these files are also sent to the MM mailing list.

The following existing patterns move unchanged with each entry:

MEMORY MANAGEMENT - KMEMLEAK
        Documentation/dev-tools/kmemleak.rst
        include/linux/kmemleak.h
        mm/kmemleak.c
        samples/kmemleak/kmemleak-test.c

Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Cc: Catalin Marinas <catalin.marinas@arm.com>
---

 MAINTAINERS |   17 +++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

--- a/MAINTAINERS~maintainers-classify-kmemleak-as-an-mm-component
+++ a/MAINTAINERS
